# Organizational Structure

BizQuest operates through a chapter model.

Each chapter serves a local community while following a standardized curriculum and program framework.

Every chapter includes:

* Student participants
* Chapter leaders
* Volunteer mentors
* Community partners
* Faculty advisors (where applicable)

The national organization develops curriculum, training materials, operational standards, impact reporting, partnerships, and long-term strategy while empowering chapters to address the unique needs of their own communities.

---

# Long-Term Vision

BizQuest aims to become a nationwide network of student innovators working alongside local organizations to strengthen communities through technology and entrepreneurship.

As the organization grows, chapters will collaborate across regions, share projects, mentor one another, and collectively develop solutions that address both local and global challenges.

The long-term goal is not simply to teach students business or technology. It is to cultivate a generation of young leaders who recognize problems, build thoughtful solutions, and create lasting impact in the communities around them.
